sequenceDiagram
    actor Client
    participant PostResource
    participant PostService
    participant Post
    participant JPA
    participant PostgreSQL

    Client->>PostResource: PUT /posts/{id} with Post body
    activate PostResource
    Note over PostResource: id: Long (post identifier) post: Post (updated Post object)
    
    PostResource->>PostService: updatePost()
    activate PostService
    Note over PostService: Client retrieves existing Post
    
    PostService->>JPA: findPost(Post.class, id)
    activate JPA
    
    JPA->>PostgreSQL: SELECT * FROM post WHERE id = ?
    activate PostgreSQL
    
    PostgreSQL-->>JPA: return post row
    deactivate PostgreSQL
    
    JPA->>Post: instantiate Post
    activate Post
    deactivate Post
    
    deactivate JPA
    
    PostService->>Post: setTitle(newTitle), setContent(newContent)
    activate Post
    Note over Post: Client modifies Post properties via setters
    deactivate Post
    
    JPA->>Post: detect changes via dirty checking
    activate Post
    Note over JPA: JPA detects changes and updates database
    deactivate Post
    
    JPA->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE post SET title = ?, content = ? WHERE id = ?
    activate PostgreSQL
    Note over JPA: Changes are persisted to PostgreSQL
    
    PostgreSQL-->>JPA: return update count
    deactivate PostgreSQL
    
    PostService-->>PostResource: return void
    deactivate PostService
    
    PostResource-->>Client: ResponseEntity.noContent().build()
    Note over PostResource: HTTP 204 No Content
    deactivate PostResource